\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.  When it's over my life's end time,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And I'm about to leave here,
\par To go and stand before the Lord,
\par Jesus, please, never leave me!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Oh Jesus Christ, during my death
\par I submit my soul in Thy wounds.
\par Beside Thee shall I get rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.  My sin is great, immeasurable,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 There's nothing good within me
\par For this reason I am in grief;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I fear that Thy great judgement.
\par And if I remember Thy death,
\par For that reason my soul gets what
\par May give me consolation.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.  I form part of Thine own body,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That's why I get my relief:
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Even death, misery and great pains
\par  Cannot put us asunder.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And if I die, I die for Thee,
\par For it is by Thy dear death that
\par Hath brought me eternal life.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.   Since Thou hast risen up from death,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 I'll never remain in grave.
\par I rejoice in Thy ascension.
\par Therefore I will fear nothing.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Wherever Thou art, I shall come,
\par I shall dwell with Thee for ever,
\par And so I shall be in peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   5.  I know I shall be with Jesus,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 So nothing can disturb me;
\par I'll go to sleep and sleep soundly,
\par Nobody can wake me up
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Only Jesus Christ, Son of God,
\par Who has already ope'd the Gate
\par Into His eternal peace.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

